# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# sip-01-core — Environment Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The core library runs with NO environment variables at all: every
# variable below is optional. This repo is a library — it has no server
# and no deploy target. Applications built on the core define their own
# env model on top.
#
# ─── Build-time (Vite, VITE_*) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Anything VITE_* is baked into the public bundle at build time.
# Never put secrets here.
#
# Base URL of an engine-AI proxy endpoint. Default: same-origin
# `/api/ai` — correct when the host application serves a proxy on that
# path. Hosts that cannot rewrite POST bodies can point the core at a
# proxy directly:
# VITE_ENGINE_API_BASE=https://your-host.example/api/ai

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HOST-SIDE SECRETS (not read by this repo — documented for hosts)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Providers that need credentials (engine-tier AI, Brave Search) call a
# same-origin proxy that the HOST application operates. The core never
# sees those keys. A host proxy typically holds:
#   OPENAI_API_KEY   engine-tier AI key (OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
#   BRAVE_API_KEY    Brave Search subscription token
# Users may also bring their own keys (BYOK), stored only in their own
# browser's localStorage under the sip01:* keys — see
# docs/guides/search-providers.md and docs/guides/ai-answers.md.
